      "worked": "The variable base requires $x>0$ and $x\\ne1$. Let $u=\\log_{10}x$, so $u\\ne0$. By change of base,\n\n$$\\log_x10=\\frac{\\log_{10}10}{\\log_{10}x}=\\frac1u.$$\n\n$$\\begin{align*}u-\\frac6u&=1\\\\u^2-u-6&=0\\\\(u-3)(u+2)&=0\\\\u&=3\\text{ or }-2\\\\x&=1000\\text{ or }10^{-2}\\end{align*}$$\n\nBoth values are positive and different from $1$, so both are valid.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
